{"result":"{
  "id": "18169",
  "key": "SFCC-106",
  "summary": "Consent Gating for PWA-Loaded Tracking & Personalisation Components",
  "description": "\\*\\*As a\\*\\* Shopper,\n\\*\\*I want\\*\\* the site to respect my cookie consent preferences for tracking and personalisation features,\n\\*\\*so that\\*\\* my browsing activity is only tracked in line with my consent choices and the applicable rules for my region.\n----\nSeveral components loaded directly by the PWA fire tracking events or personalise content based on browsing behaviour. Each must only activate after the customer has accepted the relevant Didomi cookie category. The applicable category and default consent state differs per storefront.\nComponents in scope for consent gating (Accenture build scope):\n- Recently Viewed — category TBC (currently not consent-gated on Magento)\n- \\*\\*Guest Shopper:\\*\\* Given a guest shopper has given consent and browses products within a session, when they navigate to a page with the Recently Viewed rail, then products viewed during that session are shown. When the browser session ends, the history is cleared.\n- \\*\\*Guest Shopper:\\*\\* Given a guest shopper has not given consent and browses products within a session, when they navigate to a page then there is no Recently Viewed rail. \n- Einstein Recommendations — Analytics\n- Crazy Egg heatmapping — Analytics\n- Optimizely A/B testing — Analytics (US storefront only)\n- Measmerize size widget — Marketing (category TBC)\n- Narvar EDD widget — Performance (category TBC)\n- Vimeo product videos — TBC (full gate or dnt=1 fallback?)\n- Emarsys Web Extend — TBC (not yet on Consent Management page)\nOut of scope: GTM-managed tags (GA4, Facebook Pixel, Pinterest, TikTok, Google Ads, Inside Chat) — Tell No Lies scope.\nThis story is blocked pending the outcome of the consent review being conducted by Tell No Lies and Vicky Routley. That review will confirm the Didomi category for each component and the correct default consent state per storefront.\nNote: the current Magento behaviour for some components (e.g. Recently Viewed) does not consent-gate correctly. This story represents a deliberate improvement over the current like-for-like setup.\nReference: Consent Management Business Overview — [https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/299433985](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/299433985)",
